G4005.d:
πεντηκοστός, -ή, -όν 
 [in LXX for חֲמִישִׁי, חֲמִישִׁי, Lev.25:10-11, 4Ki.15:23 15:27; 1Ma.4:1-61, 2Ma.14:4; ἡ π., Tob.2:1, 2Ma.12:32 * ;] 
fiftieth. As subst., ἡ π.; 
  (a) (sc. μερίς), at Athens, a tax of two per cent.; 
  (b) (sc. ἡμέρα, i.e. the fiftieth day after the Passover), Pentecost, the second of the three great Jewish feasts (To, 2Mac, ll. with; ἑορτὴ ἑβδομάδων, Deu.16:10, al.) : Acts.2:1 20:16, 1 Cor.16:8.†
 (AS)

G4008.d:
πέραν 
 adv., [in LXX for עֵבֶר and cognate forms ;] 
on the other side, across (usually with the idea of water lying between); 
  (a) as in the older poets, as prep. with genitive: τ. θαλάσσης, John.6:1, 17 6:22, 25; τ. Ἰορδάνου, Matt.4:15 (LXX), Matt.4:25 19:1, Mark.3:8 10:1, John.1:28 3:26 10:40; τ. χειμάρρου τ. Κέδρων, John.18:1; 
  (b) τὸ π., the region beyond, the other side: Matt.8:18, 28 14:22 16:5, Mark.4:35 5:21 6:45 8:13; τ. θαλάσσης, Mark.5:1; τ. λίμνης, Luke.8:22.†
 (AS)

G4009.d:
πέρας, -ατος, τό
 (πέρα, beyond), [in LXX chiefly for קֵץ, קָצָה and cognate forms ;] 
an end, limit, boundary; 
  (a) of space: chiefly in pl., τὰ π. τ. γῆς, Matt.12:42, Luke.11:31; τ. οἰκουμένης, Rom.10:18 (LXX); 
  (b) (opposite to ἀρχή) the end: with genitive, ἀντιλογίας, Heb.6:10.†
 (AS)

G4016.d:
περι-βάλλω 
 [in LXX chiefly for כָּסָה pi., also for לָבַשׁ, עָטָה, etc. ;] 
to throw around or over, put on or over; 
  (a) of siege or defen­sive works: χάρακά σοι, Luke.19:43 (WH, mg.; παρεμβ-, WH, txt.); 
  (b) of clothing, to put on, wrap about, clothe with: with accusative of thing(s), Luke.23:11; with accusative of person(s), Matt.25:36, 38 25:43; with dupl. accusative (not cl.; Bl., § 34, 4), John.19:2; pf. pass., to have wrapped round one: with accusative of thing(s) (cl.), Mark.14:51 16:5, Rev.7:9, 13 10:1 11:3 12:1 17:4 18:16 19:13; with dative of thing(s), Rev.4:4 (WH, txt.; before ἐν, WH, mg.); fut., before ἐν (of. Deu.22:12, Ps.45:9, 13), Rev.3:5. Mid., to clothe oneself, wrap round or put on oneself: absol., Matt.6:29, Luke.12:27, Rev.3:18; with accusative of thing(s), Matt.6:31, Acts.12:8, Rev.19:8.†
 (AS)

G4061.d:
περι-τομή, -ῆς, ἡ
 (περιτέμνω), [in LXX: Gen.17:13, Exod.4:25-26 (מוּל ni., מוּלָה), Jer.11:16 * ;] 
circumcision; 
  (a) of the rite itself : John.7:22-23 Acts.7:8, Rom.4:11, Gal.5:11, Phil.3:5; 
  (b) of the state of circumcision: Rom.2:25-28 3:1, 1 Cor.7:19, Gal.5:6 6:15, Col.3:11; ἐν π. ὤν, Rom.4:10; 
  (with) by meton., π. = οἱ περιτμηθέντες, the circumcised: Rom.3:30 4:9, 12 15:8, Gal.2:7-9, Eph.2:11; οἱ ἐκ τῆς π., of Jews, Rom.4:12; of Jewish Christians, Acts.11:2, Gal.2:12, Titus.1:10; οἱ ἐκ π. πιστοί, Acts.10:45; οἱ ὄντες ἐκ π., Col.4:11 Metaphorical, Rom.2:29, Col.2:11, Phil.3:3.†
 (AS)

G4088.d:
πικρία, -ας, ἡ
 (πικρός), [in LXX chiefly for מַר and cognate forms ;] 
bitterness; 
  (a) of taste (Arist., Jer.15:17, al.); 
  (b) metaphorically, of temper, character, etc.: Rom.3:14 (LXX), Eph.4:31; ῥίζα πικρίας, Heb.12:15; χολὴ π., a malignant disposition, Acts.8:23.†
 (AS)

G4094.d:
πίναξ, -ακος, ὁ 
 [in LXX: 4Ma.17:7 R * ;] 
prop., a board, plank; hence, of various at wooden articles; 
  (a) a tablet; 
  (b) a disc, a dish: Matt.14:8, 11, Mark.6:25, 28 Luke.11:39.†
 (AS)

G4137.d:
πληρόω, -ῶ 
 [in LXX chiefly for מָלֵא ;] 
  1. to fill, make full, fill to the full, with accusative; 
  (a) of things : pass. (σαψήνη, φάραγξ), Matt.13:48, Luke.3:5" (LXX) ; figuratively, Matt.23:32; but chiefly of immaterial things: πᾶσαν χρείαν, Phil.4:19; ἦχος ἐλήρωσε τ. οἶκον, Acts.2:2; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Acts.5:28; pass., before ἐκ, John.12:3 (cf. B1., § 36, 4); π. τ. καρδίαν, John.16:6, Acts.5:3; metaphorically, of the all-pervading activity of Christ, Eph.4:10; mid., Eph.1:23; 
  (b) of persons: to fill with, cause to abound in : with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Acts.2:28 (LXX), Rom.15:13; pass., to be filled with, abound in: Eph.3:19, Phil.4:18; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), Acts.13:52, Rom.15:14, 2 Tim.1:4; with dative (Æsch., al.), Luke.2:40 (with genitive, T), Rom.1:29, 2 Cor.7:4; with accusative (so in π., see MM, xx), Phil.1:11, Col.1:9; before ἐν, Eph.5:18, Col.2:10. 
  2. to complete; 
  (a) to complete, fulfil: of number, Rev.6:11, WH, tat.; of time (MM, xx), Mark.1:15, Luke.21:24, John.7:8,  Acts.7:23, 30 9:23 24:27; ἐυδοκίαν, 2 Thess.1:11; τ. χαράν, Phil.2:2; pass., John.3:29 15:11 16:24 17:13, 1 John.1:4, 2 John.12; τ. ἔργα, Rev.3:2; ἡ ὑπακυή, 2 Cor.10:6; τ. πάσχα, Luke.22:16; 
  (b) to execute, accomplish, carry out to the full: Matt.3:15, Luke.7:1 9:31, Acts.12:25 13:25 14:26 19:21, Rom.8:4 13:8 15:19, Gal.5:14, Col.1:25 4:17, Rev.6:11, T, WH, R, mg.; 
  (with) of sayings, prophecies, etc., to bring to pass, fulfil: Matt.1:22 2:15, 17 2:23 4:14 5:17 8:17 12:17 13:35 21:4 26:54, 56 27:9, Mark.14:49 15:28 (WH, R, txt. om.), Luke.1:20 4:21 24:44, John.12:38 13:18 15:25 17:12 18:9, 32 19:24, 36, Acts.1:16 3:18 13:27, Jas.2:23 (cf. Lft., Col., 255 ff.).†
 (AS)

G4152.d:
πνευματικός, -ή, -όν
 (πνεῦμα), 
  1. of or caused by the wind, air or breath (Arist., al.). 
  2. spiritual (opposite to σωματικός, Plut.); 
  (a) of created beings : τὰ π. (RV, the spiritual hosts), Eph.6:12; of that which is related to the human spirit, opposite to ψυχικός, 1 Cor.15:44 15:46; 
  (b) of that which belongs to or is actuated by the Divine Spirit; 
  α of persons : 1 Cor.2:15 3:1 14:37, Gal.6:1; οἶκος π., figuratively, 1 Pet.2:5; 
  β of things : Rom.1:11 7:14, 1 Cor.2:13 10:3-4 12:1 14:1, Eph.1:3 5:19, Col.1:9 3:16, 1 Pet.2:5; opposite to τ. σαρκικά, Rom.15:27, 1 Cor.9:11.†
 SYN.: ψυχικός, which see, and cf. DB, ii, 410, iv, 612  (AS)

G4153.d:
πνευματικῶς 
 adv. (πνεῦμα), 
spiritually; 
  (a) by the aid of the Holy Spirit: 1 Cor.2:13 (WH, mg.), 1 Cor.2:14; 
  (b) in a spiritual sense : Rev.11:8.†
 (AS)

G4159.d:
πόθεν 
 adv., 
whence; 
  (a) of place: Matt.15:33, Luke.13:25, 27, John.3:8 6:5 8:14 9:29-30 19:9, Rev.7:13; metaphorically, of condition, Rev.2:5; 
  (b) of origin: Matt.13:27, 54 13:56 21:25, Mark.6:2, Luke.20:7, John.2:9, Jas.4:1; of parentage, John.7:27-28; 
  (with) of cause: Mark.8:4 12:37, Luke.1:43, John.1:49 4:11.†
 (AS)

G4169.d:
ποῖος, -α, -ον 
 interrog. pronom. adj. (corresponding to the demonstr. τοῖος and the relat. οἷος), [in LXX chiefly for זֶה אֵי־ ;] 
of what quality or sort: absol., n. pl., Luke.24:19; with subst.; 
  (a) prop., in direct questions: Matt.19:18 21:23 22:36 24:42, Mark.11:28 12:28, Luke.6:32-34, John.10:32, Acts.4:7 7:49, Rom.3:27, 1 Cor.15:35, Jas.4:14 (but see: ποία), 1 Pet.2:20; 
  (b) in indirect questions = ὁποῖος : Matt.21:24, 27 24:43, Mark.11:29, 33, Luke.12:39 20:2, 8, John.12:33 18:32 21:19 Acts.23:34, 1 Pet.1:11, Rev.3:3; ποῖας (sc. ὁδοῦ), Luke.5:19.†
 (AS)

G4190.d:
πονηρός, -ά, -όν
 (πονέω, to toil), [in LXX chiefly for רַע ;] 
  1. 
  (a) of persons, oppressed by toils (Hes.); 
  (b) of things, toilsome, painful (καιρός, Sir.51:12): Eph.5:16 6:13 Rev.16:2. 
  2. bad, worthless; 
  (a) in physical sense: καρπός, Matt.7:17-18; 
  (b) in ethical sense, bad, evil, wicked; 
  (α) of persons: Matt.7:11 12:34-35 18:32 25:26, Luke.6:45 11:13 19:22, Acts.17:5, 2 Thess.3:2, 2 Tim.3:13; γενεά, Matt.12:39, 45 16:4, Luke.11:29; πνεῦμια, Matt.12:45, Luke.7:21 8:2 11:26, Acts.19:12-13, 15-16; as subst., οἱ π., opposite to δίκαιοι, Matt.13:49; to ἀγαθοί, Matt.5:45 22:10; οἱ ἀχάριστοι καὶ π., Luke.6:35; sing., ὁ π., Matt.5:39, 1 Cor.5:13; id. esp. of Satan, the evil one, Matt.5:37 6:13 (see Lft., Notes, 125 ff.; but cf. McN, in l) Matt.13:19, 38, Luke.11:4 (WH, R, om.), John.17:15, Eph.6:16, 2 Thess.3:3 (Lft., Notes, l.with), 1 John.2:13-14 Jn 3:12 Jn 5:18-19; 
  (β) of things: Matt.5:11 12:35 15:19, Luke.6:22, 45, John.3:19 7:7, Acts.18:14 25:18, Gal.1:4, Col.1:21, 1 Tim.6:4, 2 Tim.4:18, Heb.3:12 10:22, Jas.2:4 4:16, 1 John.3:12, II Jn 11, 3 John.10; ὀφθαλμός (which see), Matt.6:23 20:15, Mark.7:22, Luke.11:34; as subst., neut., τὸ π., Acts.28:21, 1 Thess.5:22; opposite to ἀγαθόν, Luke.6:45, Rom.12:9; pl., Matt.9:4, Mark.7:23, Luke.3:19.
 † SYN.: see: ἄθεσμος  (AS)

G4250.d:
πρίν 
  1. as adv. of time, before, formerly (cl.; 3Ma.5:28 3Mac 6:4 3Mac 6:31)
  2. As conic. (cl.), before; 
  (a) after a positive sentence, with accusative and inf.: Matt.26:34, 75, Mark.14:72, Luke.22:61, John.4:49 8:58 (where D. om. γενέσθαι and π. becomes prep. with genitive; see Bl., § 69, 7) John.14:29, Acts.2:20" (LXX), WH, txt.; πρὶν ἤ (not such good Attic in this construction; see Bl., l.with), Matt.1:18 Mark.14:30, Acts.2:20, WH, mg., Acts.7:2; 
  (b) after a negative sentence, πρὶν ἤ: a. subjc. (before ἄν, M, Pr., 169), Luke.2:26; with optative, Acts.25:16.†
 (AS)

G4253.d:
πρό 
 prep. with genitive,  [in LXX chiefly for פָּנִים ;] 
before; 
  (a) of place: Acts.12:6, 14 14:13, Jas.5:9; π. προσώπου (= Heb. פָּנִים, Deu.3:18, Mal.3:1, al.; Bl., § 40, 9), Matt.11:10, Mark.1:2, Luke.1:76 7:27 9:52 10:1, Acts.14:13; 
  (b) of time: Matt.8:29 24:38, Luke.11:38 21:12, John.11:55 13:1 17:24, Acts.5:36 21:38, 1 Cor.2:7 4:5, Eph.1:4, Col.1:17, 2 Tim.1:9 4:21, Titus.1:2, Heb.11:5, 1 Pet.1:20, Ju 25; π. ἐτῶν δεκατεσσάρων, fourteen years ago, 2 Cor.12:2; π. προσώπου (see supr.), Acts.13:24; with genitive of person(s), Matt.5:12, John.5:7 10:8, Rom.16:7, Gal.1:17; with genitive art. inf. (= πρίν; M, Pr., 100; Bl., § 69, 7), Matt.6:8 Luke.2:21 22:15, John.1:49 13:19 17:5, Acts.23:15, Gal.2:12 3:23; as in late writers (resembling a Latin idiom but indepen­dent of it; B1., § 40, 5; M, Pr., 100 f.; of. Am 2Ma.15:36, and for other exx., Soph., Lex., see word), πρὸ ἓξ ἡμέρας τοῦ πάσχα, on the sixth day before the Passover, John.12:1; 
  (with) of preference: π. πάντων, Jas.5:12, 1 Pet.4:8; 
  (d) in compos., 
  α with subst., of position before: προαύλιον, πρόδρομος; priority of rank or order, προπάτωρ; anticipation, πρό γνωσις, πρό νοια; 
  β with adj., intensity, πρόδηλος; 
  γ with verb., of place, προάγω, προβαίνω; of preference, προαιρέομαι.†
 (AS)

G4314.d:
πρός, 
 prep. with genitive, dative, accusative 
  I. I. C. genitive, of motion from a place, from the side of, hence metaphorically, in the interests of, Acts.27:34 (cf. Page, in l.). 
  II. II. C. dative, of local proximity, hard by, near, at: Mark.5:11, Luke.19:37, John.18:16  20:11,  12 Rev.1:13. 
  III. C. accusative, of motion or direction towards a place or object, to, towards. 
  1. Of place, 
  (a) after verbs of motion or of speaking and other words with the idea of direction: ἔρχομαι, ἀναβαίνω, πορεύομαι,  λέγω, ἐπιστολή, etc., Matt.3:14, Mark.6:51, Luke.11:5, John.2:3, Acts.9:2, al. mult.; metaphorically, of mental direction, hostile or otherwise, Luke.23:12, John.6:52, 2 Cor.7:4, Eph.6:12, Col.3:13, al.; of the issue or end, Luke.14:32, John.11:4, al.; of purpose, Matt.26:12, Rom.3:26, 1 Cor.6:5, al.; πρὸς τό, with inf., denoting purpose (cf. M, Pr., 218, 220; Lft., Notes, 131), Matt.5:28, Mark.13:22, Eph.6:11, 1 Thess.2:9, al.; 
  (b) of close proximity, at, by, with: Matt.3:10, Mark.11:4, Luke.4:11, Acts.3:2, al.; after εἶναι, Matt.13:56, Mark.6:3, John.1:1, al.
  2. 2. Of time, 
  (a) towards (Plat., Xen., LXX: Gen.8:11, al.): Luke.24:29; 
  (b) for: πρὸς καιρόν, Luke.8:13, 1 Cor.7:5; πρὸς ὥραν, John.5:35, al.; πρὸς ὀλίγον, Jas.4:14. 
  3. Of relation 
  (a) toward, with: Rom.5:1, 2 Cor.1:12, Col.4:5, 1 Thess.4:12, al.; 
  (b) with regard to: Matt.19:8, Mark.12:12, Rom.8:31, al.; 
  (with) pertaining to, to: Matt.27:4, John.21:22, Rom.15:17, Heb.2:17 5:1; 
  (d) according to: Luke.12:47, 2 Cor.5:10, Gal.2:14, Eph.3:4 4:14; 
  (e) in comparison with: Rom.8:18. 
  IV. In composition: towards (προσέρχομαι), to (προσάγω), against (προσκόπτω), besides (προσδαπανάω) . 
 (AS)

G4352.d:
προσ-κυνέω, -ῶ
 (κυνέω, to kiss), [in LXX chiefly for שָׁחָה hith. ;] 
to make obeisance, do reverence to, worship; 
  (a) prop. (as in cl., of the gods: Hdt., Æsch., Plat., al.), of God, Christ and supra-mundane beings: absol., John.4:20 12:20, Acts.8:27 24:11, Heb.11:21 (Westc., in l), Rev.11:1; πίπτειν καὶ π., Rev.5:14; with dative (of the significance of this constr. as com­pared with the usual cl., with accusative, see Abbott, JG, 78 f.; JV, 133 ff.), John.4:21, 23, Acts.7:43, 1 Cor.14:25, Heb.1:6, Rev.4:10 7:11 11:16 13:4, 15 14:7 16:2 19:4, 10 19:20 22:8-9; with accusative (see supr.), Matt.4:10, Luke.4:8 24:52 (WH, R, mg., om.), John.4:22, 24, Rev.9:20 13:4, 8 13:12 14:9, 11 20:4; Seq. ἐπώπιον, Luke.4:7, Rev.15:4; 
  (b) as in cl., of homage to human superiors (cf. MM, xxi): absol., Matt.20:20, Acts.10:25; with dative (see supr.), Matt.2:2, 8 8:2 9:18 14:33 15:25 18:26 28:9, Mark.15:19, John.9:38; πεσὼν., Matt.2:11 4:9; ἐνώπιον τ. ποδῶν, Rev.3:9; with accusative, Mark.5:6 (dative T).†
 (AS)

G4366.d:
προσ-ρήγνυμι 
 [in Aq.: Ps.2:9 * ;] 
to break against, dash against; 
  (a) trans. (παιδία πέτραις, FlJ, Ant., ix, 4, 6); 
  (b) intrans., with dative: Luke.6:48-49 (cf. προσπίπτω).†
 (AS)

G4396.d:
προφήτης, -ου, ὁ [πρόφημι, to speak forth), 
 [in LXX chiefly for נָבִיא ;] 
one who acts as an interpreter or forth-teller of the Divine will (see Lft., Notes, 83f.; Tr., Syn., §vi), a prophet; 
  1. in cl. (Æsch., Hdt., Plat., al.), of the interpreters of oracles. 
  2. In NT,  
  (a) of the OT prophets: Matt.5:12, Mark.6:15, Luke.4:27, John.8:52, Rom.11:3, al.; 
  (b) of prophets in general: Matt.10:41 13:57 21:46, Mark.6:4, Luke.13:33, al.; 
  (with) of John the Baptist: Matt.21:26, Mark.6:15, Luke.1:76; 
  (d) of Christ: Matt.21:11, John.6:14, Acts.3:22, 23 7:37" (LXX) ; 
  (e) of Christian prophets in the apostolic age: Acts.15:32, 1 Cor.12:28, Eph.2:20, al.; 
  (f) by meton., of the writings of prophets: Luke.24:27, Acts.8:28, al.; 
  (g) of a poet: Titus.1:12 (on the use of the term in π. and Inscr., see Deiss., BS, 235f.; MM, xxii). 
 (AS)

G4413.d:
B. Superl., πρῶτος, -η, -ον, 
 [in LXX chiefly for רִאשׁוֹן, also for אֶחַד, etc. ;] 
first, 
  1. of Time or Place; 
  (a) absol., as subst., ὁ π.., Luke.14:18, John.19:32, 1 Cor.14:30; ὁ π. καὶ ὁ ἔσχατος, Rev.1:17 2:8 22:13; neut., τὸ π., opposite to τ. δεύτερον, Heb.10:9; τὰ π., opposite to τ. ἔσχατα, Matt.12:45, Luke.11:26, 2 Pet.2:20; anarth., Matt.10:2; pl., Matt.19:30, Mark.10:31, Luke.13:30; ἐν πρώτοις (EV, first of all), 1 Cor.15:3; 
  (b) as adj.: πρώτῃ; (sc. ἡμέρᾳ) σαββάτου, Mk 16:[9]; φυλακή, opposite to δευτέρα, Acts.12:10; equiv. to adv. in English, John.8:[7] 20:4, 8 Acts.27:43, Rom.10:19, 1 Tim.1:16, 1 John.4:19; = πρότερος (see infr.; cf.  M, Pr., 79; Bl, §11, 5; Thackeray, Gr., 183f.): with genitive, π. μου ἦν (my chief: Abbott, Jg., 509ff.; but cf. M, Pr., 245), John.1:15, 30; with art., Mark.14:12, Acts.1:1, al.; before ὁ δεύτερος, etc., Matt.22:25, Mark.12:20, al. 
  2. Of Rank or Dignity, chief, principal: Matt.20:27 22:38, Mark.9:35, Eph.6:2, al.; with genitive, Mark.12:28, 29 al.; πόλις (Field, Notes, 124), Acts.16:12; with art., Luke.15:22 19:47, Acts.13:50, al. 
  3. Neut., πρῶτον, as adv., first, at the first; 
  (a) of Time: Matt.8:21, Mark.4:28, al.; τὸ π., John.10:40, al.; 
  (b) of Order: Rom.3:2, 1 Cor.11:18, al. 
 (AS)

G4465.d:
ῥαβδοῦχος, -ου, ό
 (ῥαβδος, ἔχω), 
one who carries a rod or staff of office; 
  (a) an umpire or judge (Plat.); 
  (b) in late writers, a Roman lictor: Acts.16:38.†
 (AS)

G4491.d:
ῥίζα, -ης, ἡ 
 [in LXX chiefly for שָׁרַשׁ ;] 
a root: Matt.3:10, Luke.3:9; ἐκ ῥιζῶν, Mark.11:20; ῥ. ἔχειν, Matt.13:6, Mark.4:6; id. before ἐν ἑαυτῷ, figuratively, Matt.13:21, Mark.4:17, Luke.8:13. Metaphorical (as in various senses in cl.), of cause, origin, source, etc.; 
  (a) of things, ῥ. πάντων τ. κακῶν (Eur.), 1 Tim.6:10; 
  (b) of persons: of ancestors, Rom.11:16-18; ῥ. πικρίας, Heb.12:15. Of that which springs from a root, a shoot; metaphorically, of offspring, Rom.15:12 (LXX) Rev.5:5 22:16.†
 (AS)
